Brief info about Vinted&nbsp;

Our mission is to make second-hand the first choice, and we're looking for people who want to help us get there. Every day, we work together to help our members buy and sell pre-loved clothing and lifestyle items, giving each piece a second life - or even a third.
The Vinted Group is made up of three business units that support this mission:

Vinted Marketplace is Europe’s leading platform for second-hand fashion and a go-to destination for all kinds of pre-loved items, with a growing range of categories. Our platform connects millions of members across 20+ markets, helping great items find a new life.

Vinted Go enhances the shipping experience with a vast network of over 500,000 pick-up and drop-off points, partnering with more than 60 carriers across Europe, with added services like item verification for peace of mind on high-value pieces.

Vinted Pay is the newest part of the Vinted Group, dedicated to bringing secure, reliable payments to buyers and sellers across Europe. Seamlessly integrated into the Vinted app, it helps keep every transaction safe, efficient, and easy for our members.

Founded in 2008 in Lithuania, Vinted began as a way for friends to find new homes for clothes they no longer needed. In 2019, we became Lithuania's first unicorn! Today, our headquarters remain in Vilnius, and we've grown with offices across Europe, supported by a team of over 2,000 people.&nbsp;

Information about the position&nbsp;

As a Staff Engineer for Enterprise Applications, you will be the technical owner of the architecture of the third-party platforms our business runs on. This is a technical leadership role: you will set the technical vision, strategy, direction, principles and standards that keep these platforms reliable, auditable and scalable, make architecture decisions with long-term impact, and help others make good decisions without depending on you. You will deliver architecture that is live, documented and visible to others, and keep it maintained as tools and needs change, helping us rely less on external vendors and consultants.

You will join the IT Infrastructure team, which runs its systems as code, and work as an engineer rather than an administrator. The team is part of the IT domain. You will work across Finance , Legal , Security , People , IT and Engineering , partner on roadmaps, and will closely collaborate with our BO Automation team, which builds and runs automation for business operations.

&nbsp;

In this position, you’ll&nbsp;

• Define, own and evolve the vision, strategy and target architecture of our enterprise application landscape (for example Okta, NetSuite, Workday): system boundaries, sources of truth and technical ownership, looking 2+ years ahead

• Set integration architecture and principles for enterprise tools, and align with data and tech teams so that the data these integrations produce is reliable and usable downstream

• Build audit-readiness into the architecture: access controls, audit trails, segregation of duties, change management and documentation

• Assess new tools from an architecture perspective: fit with our existing portfolio, integration approach, security and total cost

• Translate business needs into architecture decisions, and challenge requirements and vendors when needed

• Run design reviews and keep decisions documented, and mentor engineers and analysts along the way

• Manage complex technical initiatives. Lead decisions through RFCs and ADRs, set up governance for reviewing and enforcing agreed architecture, and act as the final voice when technical deadlocks arise.

&nbsp;

About you&nbsp;

• Have owned the architecture of a complex multi-system enterprise landscape through a period of major change (rapid growth, an ERP migration, an IPO or an audit-readiness programme), with decisions that held up over time. Typically this means 12+ years of experience, including several at staff level or equivalent, but the track record matter
